senses.gloss:
N. of a sun-deity (accord. to Naigh. belonging to the atmosphere as well as to heaven;
and sometimes in the Veda identified with, at other times distinguished from Sūrya, ‘the Sun’, being conceived of and personified as the divine influence and vivifying power of the sun, while Sūrya is the more concrete conception;
accord. to Sāy. the sun before rising is called Savitṛ, and after rising till its setting Sūrya;
eleven whole hymns of the RV. and parts of others [e.g. i, 35; ii, 38; iii, 62, 10-12 &c.] are devoted to the praise of Savitṛ;
he has golden hands, arms, hair &c.;
he is also reckoned among the Ādityas [q.v.], and is even worshipped as ‘of all creatures’, supporting the world and delivering his votaries from sin;
the celebrated verse, RV. iii, 62, 10, called गायत्री and सावित्री [qq.vv.] is addressed to him), RV. &c. &c.
